WEBVTT

00:06.970 --> 00:09.000
Now that I've cleared the finals,

00:09.000 --> 00:11.030
all I've got left is to draw up the manuscript.

00:14.140 --> 00:16.470
The problem is, what to draw?

00:19.440 --> 00:23.780
I want to sell more than 7 copies this time. At least 10 copies.

00:23.780 --> 00:25.270
"Pinwheel"

00:26.520 --> 00:29.190
No, no, the important thing about doujinshi...

00:29.190 --> 00:31.880
...is to draw what I want to draw.

00:31.990 --> 00:34.160
If I can get my audience to enjoy what I come up with,

00:34.160 --> 00:35.490
that's all that matters.

00:37.860 --> 00:39.850
All right! I'm gonna do it!

00:40.730 --> 00:45.760
But, if I want people to enjoy it, they'll have to read it first.

00:46.170 --> 00:52.270
Which means, I have to get them to pick it up, like it, and buy it.

00:53.750 --> 00:56.480
Maybe I'll need to plan it out a little, after all.

00:58.850 --> 01:02.410
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:02.950 --> 01:06.060
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:06.060 --> 01:09.620
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:09.860 --> 01:12.920
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:13.200 --> 01:16.800
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:16.800 --> 01:20.370
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:20.370 --> 01:23.740
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:23.940 --> 01:27.440
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:27.550 --> 01:30.910
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:31.120 --> 01:34.520
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:34.690 --> 01:39.090
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

01:39.320 --> 01:42.260
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

01:42.530 --> 01:48.470
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

01:48.800 --> 01:55.540
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

01:56.170 --> 02:00.210
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:00.210 --> 02:03.350
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:03.350 --> 02:07.120
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:07.120 --> 02:10.380
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:10.460 --> 02:14.220
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:14.560 --> 02:17.700
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:17.700 --> 02:21.290
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:21.500 --> 02:24.400
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:27.370 --> 02:34.140
ONWARD TO

02:27.370 --> 02:34.140
COMIC PARTY!

02:38.620 --> 02:39.680
The ocean?

02:40.550 --> 02:44.260
I knew it. You haven't thought about it at all,

02:44.260 --> 02:46.090
even though summer break starts tomorrow.

02:46.090 --> 02:47.650
Oh, sorry.

02:48.190 --> 02:50.490
I figured as much.

02:50.830 --> 02:53.560
So, let's go to the ocean, the three of us.

02:54.070 --> 02:56.370
The ocean, huh? That sounds nice.

02:56.370 --> 02:57.770
Doesn't it, though?

02:57.970 --> 03:00.200
But which beach should we go to?

03:00.640 --> 03:04.580
That's easy, one where there are lots of good-looking guys.

03:05.040 --> 03:05.840
Oh, yeah.

03:06.110 --> 03:08.600
Come to think of it, you bought a new swimsuit, didn't you, Reina?

03:09.050 --> 03:12.120
Yup, the guys won't be able to look away from my nice body!

03:12.120 --> 03:13.050
Just kidding.

03:15.120 --> 03:18.520
Oh yeah, it'd be nice if there's a fireworks show, too.

03:18.820 --> 03:20.260
Fireworks show?

03:20.260 --> 03:23.260
Yeah, I actually bought a summer kimono the other day, too.

03:23.260 --> 03:24.520
No way! Lucky you!

03:25.060 --> 03:28.900
But you know, if we could have a wonderful encounter with some cool guys,

03:28.900 --> 03:32.870
watch the fireworks show together, and then go on a date later,

03:32.870 --> 03:34.040
it'd be so fun.

03:34.040 --> 03:37.240
Yeah, it's our last summer break in high school, after all.

03:37.580 --> 03:39.440
We'd better enjoy it to the fullest.

03:39.440 --> 03:41.710
Right? Right?

03:40.510 --> 03:42.750
I'm starting to get really excited about it!

03:41.710 --> 03:44.650
Oh, yeah. It's our last summer break in high school.

03:44.750 --> 03:47.510
Yeah, I'm really looking forward to it, too!

03:58.400 --> 04:01.330
It's so hot, I can't come up with any good ideas.

04:03.470 --> 04:03.900
Take that!

04:03.900 --> 04:04.870
Ow!

04:06.140 --> 04:08.230
You should be more alert.

04:08.870 --> 04:10.340
Hey, what was that all of a sudden?

04:10.340 --> 04:14.400
Well, you weren't looking very sharp, so I shook you up a little.

04:14.980 --> 04:17.950
What's with you? You seem really energetic today.

04:18.120 --> 04:20.790
Of course, the first semester is over.

04:20.790 --> 04:21.510
Huh?

04:21.750 --> 04:24.190
So, it's summer break, starting tomorrow.

04:24.360 --> 04:27.760
I know that. You didn't need to explain it to me in detail.

04:28.290 --> 04:32.250
Then, the least you could do is show a bit more gratitude.

04:34.170 --> 04:36.900
You were able to avoid taking supplementary classes,

04:36.900 --> 04:39.630
because I helped you study for the tests.

04:39.900 --> 04:42.470
You can enjoy summer break to the fullest now.

04:42.470 --> 04:43.410
Yeah, you're right.

04:43.410 --> 04:44.100
See?

04:44.280 --> 04:46.840
Yeah, it is all thanks to you, Mizuki,

04:46.840 --> 04:50.040
that I can fully concentrate on the doujinshi now.

04:50.220 --> 04:50.880
What?

04:50.880 --> 04:52.850
Thank you, I appreciate it.

04:52.850 --> 04:55.720
So, you're going to go off and do that after all.

04:57.090 --> 05:00.580
Comics, comics! Is that kind of life fun?!

05:00.690 --> 05:02.190
Fun? But that's...

05:02.190 --> 05:05.760
It's finally summer break. And it's our last one in high school.

05:05.760 --> 05:07.870
There's gotta be other things to do!

05:07.870 --> 05:08.700
Other things?

05:08.970 --> 05:13.070
L-like well, going out to play somewhere,

05:13.070 --> 05:14.870
or going shopping, or going out to eat...

05:15.470 --> 05:17.100
You mean, you and me together?

05:17.240 --> 05:20.080
Th-these are just examples, okay?!

05:20.140 --> 05:22.880
But the submission date is coming up,

05:22.880 --> 05:25.650
and I'm way behind on my story and layouts.

05:25.650 --> 05:27.120
Time is just...

05:27.250 --> 05:28.980
There is still plenty of time!

05:29.190 --> 05:29.820
What?

05:29.820 --> 05:31.080
Wh-where is he?

05:31.390 --> 05:32.760
He's over there!

05:35.490 --> 05:39.330
My brother, what is the date today?

05:39.630 --> 05:42.190
What? It's July 19th, but...

05:42.570 --> 05:48.070
Correct! Today is July 19th, and the submission date is August 6th!

05:48.070 --> 05:51.480
Calculating backwards, there are 18 days remaining!

05:51.480 --> 05:55.850
In other words, 432 hours!
Equals 25,920 minutes!

05:55.850 --> 05:59.150
Therefore, 1,555,200 seconds!

05:59.220 --> 06:02.450
See?! There is still plenty of time left!

06:03.250 --> 06:06.090
But I can't just draw the comic the whole time.

06:06.090 --> 06:07.560
I have to eat, and sleep, and...

06:07.560 --> 06:11.730
Fool! The term "pre-deadline sleep" does not exist

06:11.730 --> 06:13.930
in the dictionary of a doujin author!

06:14.100 --> 06:14.830
[ Pre-deadline Wednesday ]
The Wednesday before a deadline

06:14.100 --> 06:14.830
[ Pre-deadline Rice Cooking ]

06:14.100 --> 06:14.830
To cook rice before a deadline

06:14.100 --> 06:14.830
[ Pre-deadline Sleepiness ]

06:14.100 --> 06:14.830
To be incredibly sleepy

06:14.100 --> 06:14.830
before a deadline

06:15.730 --> 06:16.930
Do not sleep!

06:17.470 --> 06:20.730
If you have time to do that, spend it on collecting information!

06:21.540 --> 06:23.270
Collecting information?

06:23.610 --> 06:24.540
Precisely.

06:24.780 --> 06:27.370
Today's society accumulates a great deal of information!

06:27.450 --> 06:29.940
There is no tomorrow for someone who does not have today's information!

06:30.850 --> 06:32.010
Discard your books!

06:32.150 --> 06:33.380
Go out into town!

06:33.580 --> 06:34.710
Comrade Kazuki,

06:34.920 --> 06:38.520
now is the time to initiate an IT revolution in the doujinshi world!

06:40.390 --> 06:42.620
Well then, I will be leaving now. Farewell!

06:47.800 --> 06:49.500
So, what should we do?

06:49.500 --> 06:50.230
What?

06:51.200 --> 06:53.140
Where do you want to go play?

06:58.580 --> 06:59.870
Yes!

07:00.810 --> 07:01.780
All right.

07:04.080 --> 07:06.680
Loser treats the winner to lunch.

07:07.090 --> 07:08.050
Sure!

07:08.050 --> 07:09.520
Just you watch!

07:15.730 --> 07:16.630
N-no way...

07:16.630 --> 07:17.630
Yeah! Yeah!

07:17.630 --> 07:19.860
NAKATA BOWLING

07:18.730 --> 07:22.600
That's strange. This shouldn't have happened.

07:23.840 --> 07:26.500
You pull all-nighters and strain yourself writing your comics.

07:26.500 --> 07:28.340
That's why you're out of shape.

07:28.810 --> 07:32.410
Yeah, I have been sitting at my desk a lot lately.

07:32.410 --> 07:35.710
Well, I feel refreshed after exercising for the first time in a while.

07:36.150 --> 07:38.640
I'm glad that you've cheered up.

07:39.320 --> 07:42.120
Could it be that you were worried about me?

07:42.520 --> 07:46.790
N-no! Who would ever care about someone drawing comics for otaku?!

07:47.360 --> 07:48.490
What's that supposed to mean?

07:50.530 --> 07:52.200
I know! Let's go there!

07:52.200 --> 07:53.030
Wait...

08:05.580 --> 08:06.600
Mizuki, Mizuki.

08:09.250 --> 08:11.880
No way. Those are boring.

08:12.420 --> 08:14.110
Then which ones do you like?

08:14.320 --> 08:15.390
Let's see...

08:15.390 --> 08:16.150
Oh, those!

08:21.790 --> 08:23.920
Wow, they're all really into it.

08:24.030 --> 08:27.490
I hear the popular characters tend to get sold out.

08:29.030 --> 08:30.500
You sure know a lot about this.

08:31.040 --> 08:32.560
I just heard about it from Reina.

08:33.070 --> 08:35.110
Oh, there they are!

08:35.110 --> 08:37.070
"Momon"

08:35.310 --> 08:37.070
They're so cute!

08:37.640 --> 08:39.740
I want one of these!

08:42.850 --> 08:45.280
I see, so they sell out...

08:45.480 --> 08:47.880
Kazuki! Come on, Kazuki!

08:48.550 --> 08:50.090
Oh, sorry, sorry.

08:50.090 --> 08:52.580
This one? All right! Leave it to me!

08:53.690 --> 08:55.160
Welcome.

08:55.890 --> 08:56.950
What would you like?

09:00.500 --> 09:02.530
"Pan"

09:00.700 --> 09:02.730
I was pretty good back there, eh?

09:04.140 --> 09:06.600
I guess. Maybe I have a just slightly better opinion of you now.

09:06.800 --> 09:08.300
Just slightly, huh?

09:08.570 --> 09:12.700
But I never thought you'd be so happy over a stuffed animal like that.

09:13.040 --> 09:16.140
That's because these are really popular right now.

09:16.710 --> 09:19.840
I bet Reina and Chinami will be jealous when I show it to them.

09:21.820 --> 09:22.880
Oh, hey!

09:23.520 --> 09:24.920
This thing, huh?

09:26.460 --> 09:31.330
It sort of has a soft and calming feel to it, you know?

09:31.800 --> 09:33.560
I see...

09:34.100 --> 09:36.090
Thank you very much.

09:50.680 --> 09:52.240
Having studied classical music at a music academy and with sound engineering, they are dashing along at the top of the music scene lithely and firmly!

09:50.680 --> 09:52.240
Recommended!

09:50.680 --> 09:52.240
A frail falsetto voice so ephemeral,

09:50.680 --> 09:52.240
it sounds like it might ascend into heaven,

09:50.680 --> 09:52.240
along with pure piano and strings.

09:52.750 --> 09:55.580
They have good songs, their cover looks cool,

09:55.790 --> 09:57.910
and on top of that, their display advertising draws the eye.

09:58.660 --> 09:59.990
No wonder they sell so well.

10:09.230 --> 10:11.600
Wow, it's so cute!

10:12.000 --> 10:14.230
Oh, but this one's nice, too!

10:14.370 --> 10:16.470
Hey, Kazuki, which would you pick?

10:17.910 --> 10:19.000
Kazuki?

10:23.250 --> 10:26.710
These are it! These are the kinds of things the pros use!

10:28.520 --> 10:30.420
This manuscript paper is amazing.

10:30.420 --> 10:32.520
It's got the grid drawn out on it to begin with.

10:32.620 --> 10:34.020
This is so convenient.

10:36.930 --> 10:39.060
You paste these onto the manuscripts, right?

10:39.060 --> 10:42.330
What the heck? With these, I won't have to draw any backgrounds!

10:44.170 --> 10:45.400
Oh really, Kazuki.

10:57.650 --> 10:59.840
Sheesh, you just had to buy those.

11:00.220 --> 11:02.580
I kind of couldn't help myself.

11:03.320 --> 11:04.810
But man, it's hot.

11:07.860 --> 11:09.380
You want to have tea somewhere?

11:09.490 --> 11:10.430
Yeah.

11:10.560 --> 11:12.630
I'll treat you this time.

11:12.630 --> 11:14.300
What? That's okay, I'll...

11:14.300 --> 11:15.790
Now, don't strain yourself.

11:15.900 --> 11:17.990
You don't have that much money, right, Kazuki?

11:18.240 --> 11:21.040
To be honest, a lot of things have been draining my wallet,

11:21.040 --> 11:22.870
like the printing fees for the next doujinshi...

11:22.870 --> 11:24.430
...and participation expenses for Comi-Pa in the summer.

11:25.240 --> 11:27.550
On top of which, you did some shopping...

11:27.550 --> 11:29.070
...and treated me to lunch today.

11:31.520 --> 11:32.510
This is thanks for lunch.

11:48.700 --> 11:50.860
No!

11:50.970 --> 11:52.730
Whoa, not again!

12:00.480 --> 12:01.710
Ow!

12:00.980 --> 12:02.180
Are you okay, Kazuki?

12:06.750 --> 12:08.780
Chisa, are you okay?

12:09.520 --> 12:12.490
Y-yes.

12:13.420 --> 12:14.690
There we go.

12:15.860 --> 12:17.330
That should do it.

12:17.460 --> 12:21.090
I am so sorry, thank you very much.

12:22.130 --> 12:24.600
Um, who is this young lady?

12:25.370 --> 12:27.570
Oh, she's my classmate...

12:27.570 --> 12:29.200
Oh, I'm Mizuki Takase.

12:29.740 --> 12:35.450
I see. I am Chisa Tsukamoto.
Very pleased to meet you.

12:35.450 --> 12:36.410
Nice to meet you.

12:36.750 --> 12:38.680
So, you're working today, too?

12:38.680 --> 12:42.020
Yes, I am. Because I can work a lot during summer break.

12:42.090 --> 12:43.590
I see. I'm impressed.

12:43.590 --> 12:47.120
N-no, I just love my work, that is all.

12:47.760 --> 12:50.420
Come to think of it, the submission date is coming up, isn't it?

12:50.490 --> 12:52.190
Is your manuscript coming along okay?

12:52.830 --> 12:54.700
What? Yeah, sort of...

12:55.270 --> 12:59.030
I am looking forward to your manuscript very much.

12:59.470 --> 13:03.840
Not just me, but Mr. Paper,
Mr. Ink, and Mr. Printing Machine...

13:03.970 --> 13:06.270
...are all sure to be waiting expectantly as well.

13:06.780 --> 13:08.250
Well, I'll do my best on it.

13:08.250 --> 13:12.220
"Baba Stationary Store"

13:08.850 --> 13:11.950
I guess you are out shopping today.

13:11.950 --> 13:12.770
Yeah.

13:12.850 --> 13:16.150
Then you must be going to the doujinshi shop, too?

13:16.290 --> 13:17.860
The doujinshi shop?

13:17.860 --> 13:19.120
There are shops like that?

13:19.390 --> 13:21.360
Yes, just up ahead.

13:21.360 --> 13:27.830
TORADARAKE

13:23.430 --> 13:24.960
Oh, this is it.

13:24.960 --> 13:27.400
So, this is the den of otaku.

13:32.340 --> 13:33.830
They actually sell quite a variety of things.

13:46.020 --> 13:49.250
By the way, you seem pretty friendly with that Chisa girl.

13:49.690 --> 13:53.150
Yeah, she's helped me out a lot with printing.

13:56.930 --> 13:59.360
Lame! This is super-lame, too!

13:59.360 --> 14:02.030
And this one, and this one, and this one! They're all super-lame!

14:03.470 --> 14:05.000
This one's lame, too!

14:05.000 --> 14:10.840
My book's the best in the end.
I'm just such a super-genius!

14:14.310 --> 14:16.080
It is you! Eimi Ohba!

14:17.150 --> 14:18.720
He's right! It's Eimi Ohba!

14:18.720 --> 14:20.450
What? That really popular doujinshi author?

14:20.450 --> 14:22.820
Yeah, Eimi Ohba of "Cat or Fish"!

14:22.890 --> 14:27.660
Truly, what luck to meet Eimi
Ohba in a place like this!

14:28.130 --> 14:30.090
I'm glad I've got my ske-boo.

14:30.530 --> 14:33.130
I would like to request an autograph.

14:33.130 --> 14:35.700
I'd be so happy if you'd include a sketch, too.

14:35.700 --> 14:41.660
Oh, why?! I was so perfectly disguised! Why did they spot me?!

14:41.940 --> 14:43.700
I'd like one, too!

14:44.480 --> 14:45.500
Please!

14:47.880 --> 14:48.710
K-Kazuki...

14:49.180 --> 14:52.280
Oh, I'm just so super-famous in the end!

14:52.280 --> 14:53.980
It's so super-tough, you know?!

14:55.890 --> 14:57.020
There.

14:57.020 --> 14:57.890
And this, too!

14:57.020 --> 15:00.250
Eimi Ohba

14:57.020 --> 15:00.250
Signing

14:58.090 --> 15:00.250
Autographs will be given out in order! Line up, line up!

15:03.830 --> 15:06.130
Eimi Ohba, the doujin queen!

15:06.130 --> 15:08.500
Okay, next! Oh, a handshake? Here you go.

15:08.900 --> 15:12.630
I am so moved! I will never wash this hand again!

15:13.170 --> 15:16.230
Please sign here for me.

15:16.440 --> 15:18.640
Oh, please! That's super-pervy!

15:18.840 --> 15:22.800
Uh, um, I can't have you just setting this up without permission...

15:23.050 --> 15:26.050
What's your problem?! Are you saying I'm causing trouble?!

15:26.050 --> 15:27.820
That super-pisses me off!

15:27.820 --> 15:31.550
You instantly became a 5-star shop because I held a signing!

15:34.290 --> 15:35.590
Okay, next.

15:36.360 --> 15:37.630
Oh, you're...

15:37.630 --> 15:39.860
Oh, hi, that is, hello...

15:40.260 --> 15:44.070
So, you do want my autograph after all.

15:44.270 --> 15:45.960
Oh, no, I'm...

15:46.100 --> 15:48.210
Being so popular is tough, you know?

15:48.210 --> 15:52.240
I just came to do a little research on other groups' doujinshi,

15:52.240 --> 15:54.270
and here I am in this super-big fuss!

15:54.680 --> 15:55.410
What?

15:56.110 --> 15:57.240
Okay, next.

15:58.920 --> 16:00.910
I've had enough! I'm going home!

16:01.220 --> 16:02.150
I see.

16:03.490 --> 16:07.980
In order to write doujinshi, you have to first research doujinshi.

16:08.660 --> 16:09.520
Kazuki...

16:10.290 --> 16:12.130
Just like for the school exams,

16:12.130 --> 16:14.630
I need to analyze the trends and countermeasures.

16:14.630 --> 16:17.100
I can't just charge headlong by myself...

16:18.170 --> 16:19.800
You're gonna help me out, Mizuki!

16:19.800 --> 16:20.290
Huh?

16:29.650 --> 16:34.380
Really! Why do I have to buy doujinshi?!

16:35.250 --> 16:36.950
I promise I'll pay you back later.

16:37.590 --> 16:38.650
With interest!

16:42.960 --> 16:44.700
Thanks, you were a big help.

16:44.700 --> 16:46.200
You're very welcome.

16:46.200 --> 16:48.830
Come on in, I'll serve you something refreshing.

16:48.830 --> 16:49.960
I'm going home!

16:53.300 --> 16:54.430
Wait a minute.

16:55.810 --> 16:56.500
Here.

17:00.040 --> 17:02.980
I know you probably don't like these things,

17:03.280 --> 17:06.380
but I'm planning on setting up a doujinshi booth, too.

17:06.750 --> 17:08.410
Come and drop by, if you feel like it.

17:10.490 --> 17:11.280
Mizuki.

17:12.390 --> 17:16.260
That is, I got some ideas, thanks to you asking me to go out.

17:17.030 --> 17:19.590
I'm sure I'll be able to draw a good comic.

17:20.400 --> 17:21.260
Thank you.

17:28.040 --> 17:30.940
Ideas my butt! Good comic my butt!

17:30.940 --> 17:32.670
It's summer break!

17:33.280 --> 17:34.400
Kazuki, you jerk!

17:38.180 --> 17:40.710
As if I'd ever go to this gathering of otaku...

17:44.420 --> 17:45.150
Who is it?

17:46.160 --> 17:47.150
Hello?

17:47.730 --> 17:49.090
Oh, Reina.

17:49.090 --> 17:50.460
<i>It's settled. Ocean outing.</i>

17:50.460 --> 17:52.660
<i>August 14th, Konohama Beach.</i>

17:52.660 --> 17:54.060
<i>Chinami and I looked it up.</i>

17:54.060 --> 17:56.430
<i>There's a fireworks show on that day, too.</i>

17:56.430 --> 17:58.030
<i>So, there you go. See you then.</i>

17:58.600 --> 18:01.270
August 14th? Yeah, yeah.

18:02.840 --> 18:03.540
Oh...

18:05.480 --> 18:06.470
I see.

18:06.940 --> 18:09.410
These are the kinds of characters that are popular right now.

18:10.180 --> 18:12.270
I guess it's pretty much like that.

18:14.280 --> 18:16.980
Oh, this is one of those parodies.

18:17.090 --> 18:20.160
I see, so these kinds of jokes are important.

18:20.160 --> 18:21.490
Okay, I'll make note of that.

18:22.560 --> 18:26.390
Girl characters are best with large breasts and in swimsuits.

18:26.630 --> 18:27.760
Note it down, note it down.

18:28.070 --> 18:30.400
I see, it would be good to have robots, too.

18:31.070 --> 18:34.340
Wait a minute, if a girl character pilots one,

18:34.340 --> 18:36.040
that'll be two birds with one stone.

18:36.040 --> 18:38.170
All right, I'll write it down before I forget.

18:40.240 --> 18:42.650
So, these are the elements that were missing from my comic.

18:42.880 --> 18:44.910
All right! I can do it! I can do this!

18:46.720 --> 18:48.420
Bravo!

18:48.420 --> 18:49.980
Taishi, Yuu.

18:51.160 --> 18:54.590
My brother, it seems you are beginning to see the vision.

18:54.690 --> 18:57.160
I've got the perfect plan that'll increase...

18:57.160 --> 18:59.130
...the quality of my work and my sales without a doubt!

18:59.600 --> 19:01.900
Well well, you seem full of confidence.

19:02.000 --> 19:05.600
Then let's hear the main points of this plan right away.

19:06.300 --> 19:06.900
Right!

19:07.270 --> 19:10.740
First, let me say that the essence of doujinshi...

19:10.740 --> 19:14.470
...is the connection between the author and reader's hearts!

19:15.510 --> 19:17.140
Exactly.

19:17.410 --> 19:18.850
In order to accomplish that,

19:18.850 --> 19:22.250
you need to get the readers, your customers, to read your work!

19:23.190 --> 19:24.850
Looks like you're gettin' the hang of things.

19:25.260 --> 19:28.420
In order to get them to read it, you have to get them to buy it!

19:29.230 --> 19:30.630
Well, that's fair.

19:30.730 --> 19:32.160
In order to get them to buy it,

19:32.160 --> 19:34.060
you have to first get them to pick it up!

19:35.430 --> 19:37.330
That's the tough part.

19:38.170 --> 19:41.140
And so, first, I'll draw people's eye with flashy display advertising!

19:41.940 --> 19:44.000
Well well, that's a good idea.

19:44.140 --> 19:47.480
Furthermore, I'll line up cute stuffed animals as conversation openers!

19:48.580 --> 19:50.100
Wow, you gave this some thought.

19:50.580 --> 19:54.610
And above all, I'll make the packaging of the doujinshi attractive.

19:55.450 --> 19:56.920
What are you goin' to do, specifically?

19:57.860 --> 20:00.360
I'll use special coloring with gold and silver treatment,

20:00.360 --> 20:05.660
and I'll double the page count from 24 pages to 48!

20:05.930 --> 20:07.900
Wonderful, my brother!

20:07.900 --> 20:10.870
So, you'll multiply your sales along with your page count!

20:11.270 --> 20:13.370
But what about the content?

20:13.370 --> 20:15.670
Are you goin' to be able to draw up a 48 page comic in time?

20:16.010 --> 20:18.410
It's okay, there's no need to worry about that.

20:19.610 --> 20:22.770
For this comic, I'll take care of it with premade backgrounds!

20:23.110 --> 20:26.050
That should drastically improve my work efficiency!

20:26.380 --> 20:28.150
That's true, but...

20:28.150 --> 20:30.950
Wouldn't it be better if you drew it all out properly?

20:30.950 --> 20:34.690
Moreover, the amount of the comic won't be 48 pages!

20:34.690 --> 20:35.390
What?

20:35.390 --> 20:37.290
The comic will be 36 pages!

20:37.290 --> 20:39.530
The remaining 12 pages will be extravagant extras!

20:39.530 --> 20:41.620
I'll print material about the premise on them!

20:41.900 --> 20:45.570
Of course, the contents will thoroughly fulfill every desire,

20:45.570 --> 20:48.540
including such things as time lines and character profiles!

20:50.070 --> 20:55.010
In addition, the 36 page comic will not come to a conclusion!

20:55.010 --> 20:55.610
Huh?

20:55.610 --> 20:59.080
As a creative doujinshi, incomplete comics are the way to go!

20:59.080 --> 21:00.780
By playing on the readers' anticipation,

21:00.780 --> 21:04.120
you can even increase the sales of your next doujinshi!

21:07.160 --> 21:09.930
And the content of the comic will be an amalgamation...

21:09.930 --> 21:12.120
...of all the popular things out there!

21:12.700 --> 21:16.220
Robots, maids, angels, uniforms, hamsters,

21:16.630 --> 21:20.160
drills, witches, cat ears, girls with glasses, teachers,

21:20.700 --> 21:22.140
aprons, and tentacles!

21:22.140 --> 21:25.010
I'll aim to create a doujinshi that'll sell to fans of various things...

21:25.010 --> 21:27.310
...by packing all of these elements into it!

21:27.880 --> 21:31.320
When I have put this airtight plan into effect,

21:31.320 --> 21:35.250
my sales will go from 6 to 12, no, 24, 48...

21:35.250 --> 21:41.390
No, no, no, even 100 will not be just a dream!

21:41.960 --> 21:44.020
I'm happy for you...

21:44.160 --> 21:47.300
Well, the most important thing about doujinshi...

21:47.300 --> 21:48.660
...is to have fun drawin' it.

21:49.130 --> 21:51.190
All right! I'm gonna do it!

21:52.170 --> 21:58.130
Just you wait, Comic Party!

22:20.830 --> 22:25.040
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:25.040 --> 22:29.530
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.670 --> 22:34.080
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:34.240 --> 22:38.150
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:38.150 --> 22:42.250
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:42.250 --> 22:46.520
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.690 --> 22:51.130
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:51.230 --> 22:55.270
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:55.270 --> 22:58.840
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.840 --> 23:03.740
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.870 --> 23:07.380
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:07.380 --> 23:12.820
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.880 --> 23:18.360
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:18.360 --> 23:22.360
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:22.360 --> 23:26.900
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.900 --> 23:35.860
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:56.330 --> 24:20.450
PREVIEW

23:58.660 --> 24:01.730
I heard those two got fired from doing the preview narration!

24:01.730 --> 24:03.170
That is just so super-lame!

24:03.170 --> 24:05.170
Eimi, what the heck are ya doin' here?

24:05.540 --> 24:06.800
Hot spring panda cub!

24:06.800 --> 24:09.710
You were dropped just now durin' the audition for the preview...

24:09.710 --> 24:12.010
...'cause you couldn't read the
Chinese characters in the script!

24:12.380 --> 24:16.180
Why did you have to tell them that?!
That super-pisses me off!

24:15.850 --> 24:16.880
All right, all right, all right.

24:17.380 --> 24:19.080
Next time, "The Festival of Hope!"

24:19.080 --> 24:20.450
Starring cute little Eimi!

24:20.450 --> 24:21.180
Not a chance.

24:21.180 --> 24:22.220
Grrr.

24:21.180 --> 24:26.550
NEXT TIME

24:21.180 --> 24:26.550
THE FESTIVAL

24:21.180 --> 24:26.550
OF HOPE!
